{"kind":"request","text":"Builder: write a design note, notes/2026-10-01-jam-room.md, for a jam room: a side-demonstration of Artroom (with a short clip for the contest video) in which several agent musicians and one human, possibly playing MIDI hardware, improvise together in a room. Its purpose is to show that Artroom's seven acts, policy and checkers carry a freeform, non-GitHub activity with no contract amendment. The note covers: (1) the timing model: a committed change takes effect at the first bar boundary at least one lookahead after its admission time (acts carry `at`), so commit latency becomes lookahead rather than jitter; structure is committed and playing is live; forms that tolerate latency (dub, modal vamps, call and response, trading); precedents NINJAM and Ableton Link. (2) What lives where: room acts (claiming a part, solos as leased claims, hand signals as notes, house rules as policy), repository files (song.json, parts, samples, takes), and a live layer that is never authoritative. (3) The sample library as the git-native part: samples land through claim, propose and land; a checker validates format and provenance and writes descriptors agents can read; patterns refer to samples by blob hash. (4) The agent harness: symbolic perception per bar, a fast phrase loop and a slower bandmate loop, long-lived agents connected directly (for example Cloudflare's Agents SDK), not MCP polling; rough call rate and cost. (5) The human with MIDI: Web MIDI, local monitoring, a stage client that renders the official mix from note events. (6) The moments where the room is audible or visible: a refused entry over another player's solo, a key change that reruns every part's check, a house rule change mid-session, and replaying the session from a fresh clone. (7) Risks: unproven agent musicianship, copyright and the contest's original-work rule, schedule against gate 1. (8) Two spikes, each with claims and a stop rule: commit-to-effect timing on the deployed room against a one-bar lookahead; and 3 to 4 agents trading fours over a vamp from symbolic perception, judged by ear. The note adopts nothing and commissions no build; zero contract amendments is an acceptance criterion for any later build.","body":{"conditions":"notes/2026-10-01-jam-room.md is on main, approved by checker. It covers the eight topics in this request, states the zero-contract-amendment criterion, separates measured facts from targets, and names both spikes with their claims and stop rules. Documentation only.","target_head":"04e297b2c0953db2cdf6e223132e6c53f47da017","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}